-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",178,{
[5665]="70001711\n1\tDefeat Fûshath the Beast\tFûshath the Beast can often be found in the neighbourhood east of Una's allies. Enan has tasked you with defeating Fûshath the Beast, the mighty Gorthorog enforcer.\n2\tTalk to Enan\tEnan is by Una's allies, in the city of Donnvail, west of the neighbourhood where Fûshath the Beast could once be found. You should return to Enan with news of your victory.\n",
[5666]="70022B30\n1\tDefeat Gaerdring\030Defeat Gaerthel\tGaerdring and Gaerthel, ancient warrior brothers, have arisen deep within the maze of the Great Barrow.\n",
[5667]="70001206\n1\tFind Gaeruan's nest in Duvuinen\tGaeruan's nest is resting in the middle of the lake Duvuinen, north of Gabilshathûr. The caves of Grishbalt are north-east of Gaeruan's nest. Take one of Gaeruan's eggs from her nest and place it near the central bonfire in the caves of Grishbalt.\n2\tTalk to Guard Ansurr\tGuard Ansurr can be found in the dwarf-holding of Gabilshathûr, south-west of Grishbalt. Guard Ansurr's plan worked perfectly. The mother-turtle was drawn into the caves, and her rage threw the camp into confusion.\n",
[5668]="70024FE1\n1\tFind out what the mayor wants from you\tThe mayor stands in the centre of Winter-home, overseeing the events of the Yule Festival. You should speak with the mayor and find out what he wants from you, though it sounds like he has a sleazy scheme brewing.\n2\tConvince Gareth Rust to confide in you\tGareth Rust is in the workers' area in Winter-home, toiling unhappily with his fellow workers. You should try to get some dirt on Gareth Rust, as his negativity makes him a candidate for being let go.\n3\tTry to convince Daley Utteridge to confide in you (outsider though you are)\tDaley Utteridge stands near Gareth Rust in the workers' area. You should see if Daley Utteridge will trust you enough to speak of the workers' unhappiness to an outsider.\n4\tTalk to Daley Utteridge -- maybe he will talk back\tDaley Utteridge is in the workers' area of Winter-home. You should try to persuade Daley Utteridge to tell you more so that the mayor will have the information he seeks. To perform an emote, select your target and type the required emote in your chat window. (Example: '/cheer')\n5\tOffer comfort and pat Daley Utteridge on the head\tDaley Utteridge is in the workers' area of Winter-home. You should try to persuade Daley Utteridge to tell you more so that the mayor will have the information he seeks. To perform an emote, select your target and type the required emote in your chat window. (Example: \"/cheer\")\n6\tSigh your sympathy at Daley Utteridge\tDaley Utteridge is in the workers' area of Winter-home. You should try to persuade Daley Utteridge to tell you more so that the mayor will have the information he seeks. To perform an emote, select your target and type the required emote in your chat window. (Example: '/cheer')\n7\tSee if Daley Utteridge will tell you anything useful\tDaley Utteridge is in the workers' area of Winter-home. You should speak with Daley Utteridge and see if he will share the information that the mayor seeks.\n8\tTell Mayor Goodnough everything you learned from Daley Utteridge\tThe mayor is in the centre of town among the festival patrons. You should tell Mayor Goodnough what Daley Utteridge told you concerning Gareth Rust and the record of unsavoury transactions that now lies in his hands.\n9\tUse the summoning horn to call the mayor and protect him from the workers' wrath\tThe mayor wishes for you to meet the two workers in the woods south-east of town. When you are ready, you should go to the woods and summon the mayor and the workers using the town's Summoning Horn.\n10\tReturn the records of corruption to Mayor Goodnough to receive your reward\tMayor Goodnough is in Winter-home in Frostbluff, awaiting news of your success in the Festival Square. You should speak with the mayor now that you have helped to save his reputation and return the stolen records to him.\n",
[5669]="7006DF09\n1\tDeliver the broken metal clubs to a collection box\030Collect broken metal clubs ([see journal]/10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire broken metal clubs.\n",
[5670]="7006DF0B\n1\tDeliver the gorgeous ears to a collection box\030Collect gorgeous ears ([see journal]/10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire gorgeous ears.\n",
[5671]="7006DF0D\n1\tDeliver the gorgeous furs to a collection box\030Collect gorgeous furs ([see journal]/10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire gorgeous furs.\n",
[5672]="7006DF0C\n1\tDeliver the gorgeous sword sheaths to a collection box\030Collect gorgeous sword sheaths ([see journal]/10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire gorgeous sword sheaths.\n",
[5673]="7006DF0A\n1\tDeliver the nasty skins to a collection box\030Collect nasty skin ([see journal]/10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire nasty skins.\n",
[5674]="7002908E\n1\tDefeat the Dragon-clan in their new settlement (total: 15)\tDragon-clan invaders roam the western reaches of Pren Gwydh freely after having settled there. You should protect the weakened peoples of Pren Gwydh by defeating the cruel folk of the Dragon-clan.\n2\tTalk to Tomos\tTomos is near the Dragon-clan's new settlement in the western reaches of Pren Gwydh. You should return to Tomos and tell him of your success against the Dragon-clan.\n",
[5675]="70028FAF\n1\tSpeak with the first White Hand Overseer\030Speak to the second Overseer\030Speak with the third Overseer\tThe White Hand Overseers can be found in the lower areas of Galtrev, guarding their four respective posts. You should speak with White Hand Overseer at the west gate to see if he needs your help.\n2\tFind out why Flint Ironheart is blocking the entire day's work\tFlint Ironheart, the Overseer at the fourth workstation, seems to be at the root of the delay in the day's productivity. You should speak with Flint Ironheart and find out if there is anything you can do to help.\n",
[5676]="700077E7\n1\tTalk to Gammy Boggs\tGammy Boggs lives on the second farm north of the road east from the centre of Staddle. Constable Redweed suggested that you speak with Gammy Boggs, if you wish to know more about what is going on in Staddle.\n",
[5677]="70060DA1\n1\tDefeat bears in Yondershire (total: 6)\030Defeat neekers in Yondershire (total: 6)\030Defeat shrews in Yondershire (total: 6)\030Defeat sickle-flies in Yondershire (total: 6)\030Defeat wolves in Yondershire (total: 6)\tCreatures for hunting can be found throughout Yondershire. You should hunt the creatures of the Yondershire for Gytha Beatbrush and prove yourself to her.\n2\tTalk to Gytha Beatbrush in Gamwich\tGytha Beatbrush can be found in the village of Gamwich. You should talk to Gytha Beatbrush in Gamwich.\n3\tDefeat Nightfell\030Defeat Scuttlechirr\030Defeat Sharpsnout\030Defeat Keenshear\030Defeat Yellowfang\tRare and fearsome creatures for hunting can be found throughout Yondershire. You should hunt the rare and fearsome creatures of the Yondershire for Gytha Beatbrush and prove yourself to her.\n4\tTalk to Gytha Beatbrush in Gamwich\tGytha Beatbrush can be found in the village of Gamwich. You should talk to Gytha Beatbrush in Gamwich.\n",
[5678]="7000B8D1\n1\tTalk to Gandalf in Rivendell\tGandalf is in Bilbo's room on the ground floor of the Last Homely House, in Rivendell. Nogmeldir has asked you to travel into Rivendell to the west of the Misty Mountains and retrieve a special draught from Gandalf the Grey.\n2\tBring Gandalf's draught to Nogmeldir\tNogmeldir is at Vindurhal in northern High-pass. Gandalf the Grey gave you a special draught he had prepared, which you should take to Nogmeldir.\n",
[5679]="7007163A\n1\tComplete 'Instance: Gaol-break'\tEbuzâm is ready to go back into Esh Mêkag to rescue as many thralls as he can. You should speak with Ebuzâm and complete 'Instance: Gaol-break'.\n2\tTalk to Ebuzâm\tYou have succeeded in causing a riot in Esh Mêkag and freeing many thralls. You should talk to Ebuzâm.\n",
[5680]="7003FF20\n1\tDefeat Wood-cutters (total: 8)\tThe gardens are one of Dol Amroth's most prized locations.\n",
[5681]="70061270\n1\tDefeat garden pests (total: 5)\030Check on beans (total: 8)\030Pick delicious berries (total: 4)\tHelp Morna \"Old Mother\" Goldworthy tend to the garden.\n2\tTalk to Morna \"Old Mother\" Goldworthy\tMorna \"Old Mother\" Goldworthy can be found in the heights of Tighfield in the southern part of town. Talk to Morna.\n",
[5682]="70066923\n1\tTalk to Miruhir\tDerva has asked you to deliver garlic scapes to her friend Miruhir. You can find Miruhir in Iáphel.\n",
[5683]="700266EA\n1\tScout Haudh Eärendur\030Scout Haudh Elendur\030Scout Haudh Valandur\030Scout Haudh Elendil\030Scout Haudh Tarondor\030Scout Haudh Eldacar\030Scout Haudh Tarcil\030Scout Haudh Arantar\tCrypts and tombs line the pathway from the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings west to the city of Annúminas. Maladan asked you to scout the entrances to several tombs and crypts within the Way of Kings.\n2\tTalk to Maladan in the Way of Kings\tMaladan is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings. Maladan will want to know the state of the tombs and crypts within the Way of Kings.\n",
[5684]="700542E7\n1\tTalk to Cannoth\tCannoth has a plan.\n2\tDefeat Khúrthak the Rent\tDefeat Khúrthak the Rent.\n3\tTalk to Cannoth further up the path\tTalk to Cannoth further up the path.\n4\tFell beast eggs destroyed ([see journal]/4)\tReach the outcropping above and destroy the fell beast eggs before they hatch. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n5\tDefeat Khatlob the Brood-mother\tDefeat Khatlob the Brood-mother.\n",
[5685]="700542EA\n1\tTalk to Cannoth\tCannoth has a plan.\n2\tDefeat Khúrthak the Rent\tDefeat Khúrthak the Rent.\n3\tTalk to Cannoth further up the path\tTalk to Cannoth further up the path.\n4\tFell beast eggs destroyed ([see journal]/4)\tReach the outcropping above and destroy the fell beast eggs before they hatch. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n5\tDefeat Khatlob the Brood-mother\tDefeat Khatlob the Brood-mother.\n",
[5686]="700542E9\n1\tTalk to Cannoth\tCannoth has a plan.\n2\tDefeat Khúrthak the Rent\tDefeat Khúrthak the Rent.\n3\tTalk to Cannoth further up the path\tTalk to Cannoth further up the path.\n4\tFell beast eggs destroyed ([see journal]/5)\tReach the outcropping above and destroy the fell beast eggs before they hatch. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n5\tDefeat Khatlob the Brood-mother\tDefeat Khatlob the Brood-mother.\n",
[5687]="700542E8\n1\tTalk to Cannoth\tCannoth has a plan.\n2\tDefeat Khúrthak the Rent\tDefeat Khúrthak the Rent.\n3\tTalk to Cannoth further up the path\tTalk to Cannoth further up the path.\n4\tFell beast eggs destroyed ([see journal]/6)\tReach the outcropping above and destroy the fell beast eggs before they hatch. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n5\tDefeat Khatlob the Brood-mother\tDefeat Khatlob the Brood-mother.\n",
[5688]="7004E4F4\n1\tTalk to Tuhâl\tYou should talk to Tuhâl, who can be found in Utterby.\n2\tCollect edible plants (total: 15)\tEdible plants can be found in the scrublands near Utterby.\n3\tBring the plants to Kúlkhur\tYou should bring the edible plants to Kúlkhur, who can be found in Utterby.\n",
[5689]="7001BE98\n1\tCollect faded parchment (total: 8)\tPieces of faded parchment can be found in Sarnúr, south of Thorin's Hall, reached through the ruins of Orodost. Rútur has asked you to recover any pieces of faded parchment you might find in Sarnúr.\n2\tTalk to Rútur in Thorin's Hall\tRútur is in Thorin's Hall, north of Sarnúr, just outside the Blue Stone Garrison. Now that you possess the pieces of faded parchment that Rútur requested you gather, you should return them to him so that he may decipher them.\n",
[5690]="7001B9CB\n1\tMake rubbing of the ancient text (total: 6)\tHaudh Methernil, The Barrow of Ringdor, The Barrow of Taradan, and Haudh Taenthod are scattered across the northern Barrow-downs. Broderic Willowmeade has asked you to recover ancient texts in Haudh Methernil, The Barrow of Ringdor, The Barrow of Taradan, and Haudh Taenthod. Using the charcoal and paper that I have provided you, take rubbings from pillars that are scattered about.\n2\tTalk to Broderic Willowmeade in Bree\tBroderic Willowmeade can be found near the Hunting Lodge at the end of the Haunted Alley in Bree. You should return to Broderic Willowmeade with the text you found.\n",
[5691]="70025EA5\n1\tMilk the cows (total: 4)\tThe cows are at a farm to the east.\n2\tThe butter-churn is near the cows on Northcotton Farm. The next step to making butter is to churn the milk.\t\n3\tBring the butter to Rosa Brockhouse\tRosa Brockhouse is at the southern part of the Northcotton Farm. Rosa Brockhouse will want to get the butter so she can finish the pies.\n",
[5692]="70044642\n1\tCollect clothing from noble chests (total: 10)\tNoble chests can be found on the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith. You should collect donated clothing from noble chests on the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.\n2\tSpeak with Habdir\tHabdir can be found within the Clothiers' Fellow-hall on the Third Circle of Minas Tirith. You should speak with Habdir.\n",
[5693]="70025E9D\n1\tGather eggs (total: 6)\tEggs can be found near the chickens on the Northcotton Farm. Rosa Brockhouse asked you to gather several eggs to help with the pie making.\n2\tBring the eggs to Rosa Brockhouse\tRosa Brockhouse is at the Northcotton Farm. Rosa Brockhouse will want to begin working with the eggs.\n",
[5694]="70025E66\n1\tCollect wheat (total: 8)\tWheat can be found in the fields of the Northcotton Farm. Rosa Brockhouse asked you to gather some wheat to make flour for pie-crusts.\n2\tBring the stalks of wheat to Edulf Tunnelly\tEdulf Tunnelly is at the windmill on the Northcotton Farm. Edulf Tunnelly will help you grind the wheat into flour.\n3\tDefeat rats at the windmill (total: 4)\tRats can be found around the windmill at the Northcotton Farm. Edulf Tunnelly asked you to drive off some rats while she grinds the wheat into flour.\n4\tTalk to Edulf Tunnelly at the Northcotton Farm\tEdulf Tunnelly is at the windmill at the Northcotton Farm. You should return to Edulf Tunnelly.\n5\tBring the flour to Rosa Brockhouse\tRosa Brockhouse is at the Northcotton Farm. Rosa Brockhouse will be pleased to see the flour you helped make.\n",
[5695]="70071776\n1\tTalk to Khagâmi\tThe Rangers plan to relocate to Gadim-ûn so they can help the Jatsakóri. You should talk to Khagâmi at the Rangers' camp to see if she would like to go to Gadim-ûn also.\n2\tTalk to Rhadrog\tKhagâmi wants to accompany you to Gadim-ûn. You should talk to Rhadrog at his camp about your next steps.\n3\tFind Abníshu, the kalorkhûn roost\tIn an effort not to put a strain on their resources, Rhadrog has asked you to go to Abníshu, a kalorkhûn roost to the west and collect some meat to bring with you to Gadim-ûn.\n4\tCollect kalorkhûn meat (total: 6)\tYou have found Abníshu, the kalorkhûn roost Rhadrog told you about. You should defeat some kalorkhûn to collect their meat to bring with you to Gadim-ûn.\n5\tFind where the sounds of combat originate\tAs you gathered kalorkhûn meat for the people of Gadim-ûn, you heard the sound of combat coming from somewhere nearby. You should find from where the sound is originating.\n6\tTalk to the dwarf\tYou have found a dwarf at Abníshu, also fighting the kalorkhûn. You should talk to him.\n7\tReturn to Gadim-ûn\tYou have gathered kalorkhûn meat for the people of Gadim-ûn, and met a dwarf, Mêshaget, along the way. You should return to Gadim-ûn in north-eastern An Shêru with the meat.\n8\tBring the kalorkhûn meat to Nabatínu\tYou have gathered kalorkhûn meat for the Jatsakóri, and returned to Gadim-ûn. You should talk to Nabatínu and give him the meat.\n",
[5696]="7006292D\n1\tCollect gloom-webs (total: 8)\tHafren has asked you to collect gloom-web from Nettinglade. Gloom-web can be found in Nettinglade, in the Old Forest.\n2\tReturn to Hafren\tYou should bring the gloom-web you collected to Hafren. Hafren is at Gerwyn's Convoy, in northern Cardolan.\n",
})
